{"name":"Light Hog Bristle","hex":"#e5ddcb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"hog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any animal belonging to the Suidae family of mammals, especially the pig, the warthog, and the boar.\n An adult swine, at or above a certain body weight.","An adult swine, at or above a certain body weight."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To greedily take more than one's share, to take precedence at the expense of another or others.","To clip the mane of a horse, making it short and bristly.\n\n (of a hedge) to trim up closely"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hog"},{"term":"bristle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stiff or coarse hair on a nonhuman mammal or on a plant.","A chaeta: an analogous filament on arthropods, annelids, or other animals."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rise or stand erect, like bristles.","To abound, to be covered with, or to have an abundance of, something, especially something jutting out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bristle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paintbrush","blocks":[{"text":"A paintbrush is a brush used to apply paint or ink. A paintbrush is usually made by clamping bristles to a handle with a ferrule. They are available in various sizes, shapes, and materials. Thicker ones are used for filling in, and thinner ones are used for details. They may be subdivided into decorators' brushes used for painting and decorating and artists' brushes used for visual art."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Paintbrushes.jpg/330px-Paintbrushes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paintbrush","wikidata":"Q193897"},{"title":"Bristle","blocks":[{"text":"A bristle is a stiff hair or feather, either on an animal, such as a pig, a plant, or on a tool such as a brush or broom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Brushbristles.jpg/330px-Brushbristles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bristle","wikidata":"Q894231"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png/120px-Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png/120px-Parts_of_a_Paintbrush.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brush parts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParts_of_a_Pa